.\nNote:\n- Evaluasi permintaan TOP Payment > 7 hari.\n- Monitor shipment Ahmedabad dan shipment lainnya dan koordinasi dengan tim\ninternal MSI\n- Follow up shipment berikutnya dari origin lain	MENAGIH VOLUME IMPORT DAN ORIGIN LAINNYA SELAIN INDIA	\N	{"location": "CITOS, JAKARTA SELATAN"}	\N	50ddd3c0-6f49-4669-bd73-4aace586cc56	2026-06-19 08:16:30.965708+00	2026-06-19 08:16:30.965708+00	\N	\N
4272bdcc-ba0a-4668-843a-11fb844cc26c	0e1840d8-e6fb-4190-bd09-88338e68b492	13e5ad68-ede8-49cf-8ea0-65b2e05ee72e	\N	\N	50ddd3c0-6f49-4669-bd73-4aace586cc56	visit	done	2026-06-03	\N	2026-06-25 09:37:47.838+00	\N	\N	\N	\N	Scope Pekerjaan MSI:\n• Support kebutuhan Import by sea China to Jakarta LCL, import EV Charging mobil\ndan proteksi Listrik\n• Support kebutuhan domestic inquiry to destination Indonesia (multimoda)\n3. Vendor:\n- Belum ada vendor forwarding karena baru akan import kedua kali\n4. Gudang:\n- Warehouse assembly dan workshop di subang\n5. Note:\n- Mekanika elektrika akan melakukan import EV Charging (merk SUNTREE) dan\nproteksi Listrik (deadline import bulan juni 2026)\n- Volume import 1-2 BL per bulan untuk HO dan mengikuti by project, dan kebutuhan\nWorkshop masih ongoing untuk import karena saat ini masih membeli local\n- Rencana akan export solar panel ke negara timur\n- Saat ini akan import dengan origin China (Ningbo, dll) jepang dan Taiwan\n- Workshop assembly dan produksi Solar Panel, metal Listrik, racking, tiang PJU\n- Pengiriman barang ke seluruh Indonesia (shipment domestic)	SUDAH OFFERING RATE DAN LOST KARENA JADINYA BORONGAN YG BISA DI ARRANGE UNDER 1CBM	\N	{"location": "OFFICE BANDUNG"}	\N	50ddd3c0-6f49-4669-bd73-4aace586cc56	2026-06-24 09:55:49.575264+00	2026-06-24 09:55:49.575264+00	\N	\N
c02717b5-8ab6-4b28-88ea-dc94240fc857	0e1840d8-e6fb-4190-bd09-88338e68b492	b1a33cd3-c023-45b0-8139-3341d703978b	\N	\N	73d32d8c-7c7b-4c85-8f8c-99d393ed90e0	visit	done	2026-07-22	15:00:00	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	Maintain the relationship with Electrum	\N	{"mom": "Participant:\\nPak Edy Siswanto (Procurement Manager), Ibu Ayu Yulianti (Senior Procurement Operation) - EKB\\nPak Vendi (GM BD), Ochi (Sales Executive) - MSI\\n1. Import Commodities\\nEKB's primary imported commodities include:\\nSpare Parts\\nBatteries\\nBattery Swapping Station (BSS) Machines for battery charging\\n2. Challenges Experienced in Previous Shipments Handled by MSI\\nEKB shared several concerns regarding previous import shipments managed by MSI:\\n\\na. SPJM (Physical Inspection)\\nOne shipment was subject to an SPJM inspection because the product description on the cargo labels did not match the description stated in the packing list.\\nDuring Customs inspection, the on-site representative of MSI was unable to adequately explain the discrepancy to Customs officers.\\nAs a result, Customs conducted a 100% physical inspection, causing a delay of approximately two days.\\nb. Additional Costs\\nEKB expects all potential additional costs to be communicated at the quotation stage whenever possible.\\nEarly visibility of possible extra charges will help EKB prepare a more accurate budget and avoid unexpected costs.\\nc. Urgent Air Shipments\\nDuring urgent shipments to the UAE (US - Iran conflict), MSI was unable to provide alternative airport routing and airline options.\\nEKB noted that two other logistics providers offered multiple routing and airline alternatives, which provided greater flexibility.\\n3. Expectations from Logistics Service Providers (LSP)\\nEKB emphasized that they are looking for a logistics partner that not only handles import operations but also possesses a good understanding of the products being imported.\\n\\nIn the event of Customs inspections (SPJM), EKB expects the logistics provider to assist Customs officers by explaining the product specifications and shipment details. EKB considers this technical support to be an important value-added service.\\n\\n4. Current Import Activities\\nThe last FCL import shipment was in March 2024.\\nSince then, EKB has primarily sourced products from local companies.\\n\\"Local purchasing\\" refers to purchasing from Indonesian companies that import products from Electrum's overseas suppliers.\\nCurrent logistics profile:\\n\\nAir freight is used for urgent shipments from China.\\nLCL shipments are generally avoided, as EKB prefers to consolidate cargo into one 20GP container whenever feasible.\\nProcurement composition:\\n80% Imported products\\n20% Local purchases\\n5. China Procurement Model\\nFor spare parts sourced from China:\\n\\nEKB purchases products directly from its approved suppliers.\\nProcurement activities are centralized through an aggregator, a company that consolidates cargo from multiple suppliers into one shipment.\\nIn Indonesia, Hon Bond Indonesia currently acts as the importer of record and manages the import process for shipments from China on behalf of EKB.\\n6. Import Strategy for 2027\\nEKB plans to begin importing directly under its own company in 2027, instead of using a trading company.\\n\\nEstimated import volume:\\n\\n30–40 containers per month\\nThis represents a significant business opportunity for logistics service providers.\\n\\n7. Immediate Business Opportunity\\nAn immediate opportunity identified during the meeting is the SNI certification process for motorcycle wheels (velg).\\n\\nEKB requested MSI to support and manage the SNI certification process.\\n\\nEKB has already identified:\\n\\nThe overseas shipper\\nProduct specifications for the items to be ordered\\n\\nAction needed:\\n1. Follow up closely on the SNI certification process for motorcycle wheels and assess whether Storbit can handle it.  \\n2.  Approach Hon Bond Indonesia to explore potential logistics collaboration and future import opportunities related to EKB's China procurement activities.\\nConclusion:\\nEKB is seeking a logistics partner that provides not only competitive pricing but also technical knowledge of imported products, proactive communication regarding potential additional costs, and strong operational support during Customs clearance.With EKB's plan to commence direct imports under its own entity in 2027, estimated at 30–40 containers per month, MSI has a significant opportunity to establish a long-term strategic partnership by demonstrating value-added logistics services and supporting current opportunities such as the SNI certification project.", "location": "Pondok Indah", "visit_type": "discovery", "point_of_meeting": "Introduce new Account Owner for Electrum group"}	\N	73d32d8c-7c7b-4c85-8f8c-99d393ed90e0	2026-08-03 08:11:28.979491+00	2026-08-03 08:11:28.979491+00	\N	\N
